0.7.6-easyos v6
* Preferences: new Conservation Mode section (above Warning). Detects
    supported laptops (Lenovo ideapad_acpi, kernel charge_control_end_threshold,
    Huawei, LG Gram, Samsung, Sony VAIO, Acer), shows ON/OFF status and
    turns it on (about 80 %) or off (100 %) immediately.

0.7.5-easyos v5
*cleanup: removed autotools/intltool build files and unused translations;
 Vala source moved to vala/

0.7.5-easyos v4
*tray tooltip shows remaining time, e.g. "63 %l - 6 hours 5 mins remaining time"

0.7.5-easyos v3
*commands run through /bin/sh -c (redirects such as > now work)
*alert levels are checked right after saving preferences

0.7.5-easyos v2
*tray bar drawn with whole numbers, so it shows in decimal-comma languages
*text mode "%" fixed

0.7.5-easyos v1
*EasyOS: detect batteries by sysfs type, skip peripheral batteries
*accept energy_*, charge_* or capacity
*plugged in + full/not charging/unknown counts as charged
*alerts via vattery-alert helper (gxmessage/yad/Xdialog/notify-send/xmessage)
*0% no longer reported as "no batteries"; guard divide-by-zero
*Quit menu item; build-easyos.sh without autotools

0.7
*added 'text mode'

0.67
*builds with vala 0.8
*works with GTK+2 2.20

0.66
*function get_battery_status now checks for multiple batteries
*added function set_tooltip_text
*added "charged" color

0.6.5
*switched build system to automake
*internationalized
*build clean on Vala 0.7.10

0.6.4
*updated to Vala 0.7.9
